ey":"/type/edition"},"description":"The first truly European history of contemporary Europe, from Lisbon to Leningrad, based on research in six languages, covering 34 countries across 60 years, using a great deal of material from newly available sources. The book integrates international relations, domestic politics, ideas, social change, economic development, and culture--high and low--into a single grand narrative. Every country has its chance to play the lead, and although the big themes are handled--including the cold war, the love/hate relationship with America, cultural and economic malaise and rebirth, and the myth and reality of unification--none of them is allowed to overshadow the rich pageant that is the whole.--From publisher description.","ocaid":"postwarhistoryof00judt","isbn_10":["1594200653"],"lccn":["2005052126"],"oclc_numbers":["61303516"],"dewey_decimal_class":["940.55"],"lc_classifications":["D1051 .J84 2005","D1051.J84 2005"],"latest_revision":19,"revision":19,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-09-29T19:58:01.955179"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-07-05T05:03:03.344766"}},{"publishers":["William Heinemann"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["4737934"],"goodreads":["1259821"]},"subtitle":"A History of Europe Since 1945","isbn_10":["0434007498"],"covers":[6953910],"physical_format":"Hardcover","key":"/books/OL22228809M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL226798A"}],"publish_places":["London"],"isbn_13":["9780434007493"],"pagination":"xv, 878 p.","classifications":{},"source_records":["marc:marc_laurentian/openlibrary.mrc:719838638:799","marc:marc_ithaca_college/ic_marc.mrc:211215111:723","bwb:9780434007493","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-012.mrc:49232234:1007","idb:9780434007493"],"title":"Postwar","dewey_decimal_class":["940.55"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},"number_of_pages":878,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["Europe -- His